  "candidate": {
    "title": "Clarify keyboard equivalents for × and ÷ operators (RQ-012)",
    "problem": "RQ-012 mandates keyboard input support for operators, but standard keyboards have no × or ÷ keys and the design does not state which physical keys (e.g., '*' and '/') should be treated as equivalents. This leaves the keyboard-operator acceptance criterion unverifiable against the design.",
    "whyUpstream": "The missing mapping is an omission in the design's RQ-012 itself; only the design authors can decide the intended key equivalents, so the specification cannot resolve this without inventing a requirement the design never states."
